<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7909bee498364736\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\ntsla-20231231\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7909bee498364736\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000162828024002390/tsla-20231231.htm\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a0cb007cc7b75c45\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nPortions of the registrant’s ... Annual Report on Form 10-K to the extent stated herein. Such proxy statement will be filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission within 120 days of the registrant’s fiscal year ended December 31, 2023. TESLA, INC....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a0cb007cc7b75c45\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sec.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f168dbd7eff6e21f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\ntsla-20240331\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f168dbd7eff6e21f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000162828024017503/tsla-20240331.htm\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"45b54806ceed8cfc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFor a description of our operating lease arrangements in Buffalo, New York, and Shanghai, China, refer to Note 15, Commitments and Contingencies, in our Annual Report on Form 10-K for the year ended December 31, 2023. As of March 31, 2024, we expect to meet the requirements under these arrangements, as may be modified from time to time, based on our current and anticipated level of operations. ... On June 4, 2018, a purported Tesla stockholder filed a putative class and derivative action in the Delaware Court of Chancery against Elon Musk and the members of Tesla’s board of directors as then constituted, alleging corporate waste, unjust enrichment and that such board members breached their fiduciary duties by approving the stock-based compensation plan awarded to Elon Musk in 2018 (the “2018 CEO Performance Award”).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"45b54806ceed8cfc\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sec.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a06f4a990bdf2efe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\ntsla-20240630\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a06f4a990bdf2efe\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000162828024032662/tsla-20240630.htm\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"53a58b6ddaf18ba7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFor a description of our operating lease arrangements in Buffalo, New York, and Shanghai, China, refer to Note 15, Commitments and Contingencies, in our Annual Report on Form 10-K for the year ended December 31, 2023. As of June 30, 2024, we expect to meet the requirements under these arrangements, as may be modified from time to time, based on our current and anticipated level of operations. ... On June 4, 2018, a purported Tesla stockholder filed a putative class and derivative action in the Delaware Court of Chancery against Elon Musk and the members of Tesla’s board of directors as then constituted, alleging corporate waste, unjust enrichment and that such board members breached their fiduciary duties by approving the stock-based compensation plan awarded to Elon Musk in 2018 (the “2018 CEO Performance Award”).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"53a58b6ddaf18ba7\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sec.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:sec.gov Tesla 10-Q 2023", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 872, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"94c8e4bd83d107ec\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n10-Q\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"94c8e4bd83d107ec\">>>", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000095017023033872/tsla-20230630.htm", "de